64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Ooh, these look interesting! But wait, Option B sounds like a nightmare for the budget and the power grid! Option A seems super safe and friendly. What do you guys think?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I agree that Option B is too risky. However, Option D is completely out of the question; we cannot have a ""working conservation bench"" when our only staff member is already drowning in a backlog of two hundred pieces.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, you're so focused on the backlog that you're missing the point. Option D puts the process on display, which is exactly the human interaction the visitors crave. It turns a failure into an attraction.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, turning a failure into an attraction does not fix the failure. Option B is impossible given our power instability, and Option D's reconstructions could easily exceed the bay's weight limit. Option A is the most logical choice.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option A sounds like a lovely way to celebrate our community. It seems much safer for our staff and building, and since the items are local, we can avoid those stressful shipping delays.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, you're so right! Local items mean way lower transport costs and probably fewer shipping headaches. Option A is looking like a winner! It's budget-friendly and won't break the bank or the building!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, @Shizue, I agree. Option A is the only sustainable choice. It avoids the conservation crisis of Option D and the technical risks of Option B, while remaining manageable for our current staff levels.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, you're choosing the path of least resistance. Option A is just more cased objects and recordings. It's a nap, not an exhibition. Option D is the only one that offers a genuine, living experience.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, your preference for ""living experiences"" ignores the reality that the building is struggling. Option D's reconstructions are a structural risk, and Option B is a technical impossibility. Option A is the only responsible decision.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I understand you want something vibrant, but we must be mindful of our friends in the lab. Option A allows us to be welcoming and joyful without placing an unfair burden on anyone.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shion, I really want it to be exciting too, but we can't ignore the facts! Option A is just so much safer for everyone. I'm voting for A to keep us all happy and solvent!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shion, it is not about the path of least resistance, but about the path of possibility. We cannot prioritize a ""living experience"" over the actual lives and well-being of our exhausted staff. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, your ""possibility"" is just a euphemism for mediocrity. You're all terrified of a little risk, but the data proves that safety is the enemy of success. I vote for Option D.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, risk is acceptable when it is calculated, but you are gambling with the building's integrity. Option A is the only proposal that ensures the gallery remains functional. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, your spirit is wonderful, but I believe the kindest choice is one where we can truly deliver on our promises. To avoid any more disappointments at the door, I also vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm so glad we could all agree on something that works for everyone! Option A is definitely the way to go. It's a win-win for the budget and the team! I'm sticking with my vote for A!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I stand by my decision. Option A is the only choice that respects our human limits and ensures the exhibition is actually achievable. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Mio, @Victoria, you've successfully voted for a snooze-fest. You've prioritized the comfort of the staff over the experience of the guests. I'll maintain my vote for Option D. Let the record show I fought for the audience.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, fighting for the audience is pointless if the gallery is closed for emergency repairs. Logic dictates that we prioritize the building's survival. My vote for Option A remains unchanged.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is a pity we could not all agree, but I believe we have made the most thoughtful choice. Let us welcome our local artisans with open arms. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
